# Day21 - Introduction to Machine Learning
Machine Learning is a method of teaching computers to learn patterns from data instead of programming them with fixed rules. In traditional programming, developers write explicit instructions for the computer to follow. However, in machine learning, we provide the computer with large amounts of data along with the correct answers, and the algorithm learns the patterns and relationships within the data. Once trained, the machine learning model can use these learned patterns to make predictions or decisions on new, unseen data. This makes machine learning very useful for tasks such as image recognition, recommendation systems, fraud detection, and speech recognition.